--- L1b NETWORK POLICY: is anything filtering the traffic? -----
    kubectl get networkpolicy (namespace imesh-demo):
          <none> - no NetworkPolicy objects exist in this namespace
    
    kubectl get networkpolicy -A (whole cluster):
          <none> - no NetworkPolicy objects exist anywhere in the cluster
    
    CNI in use:
      kindnet-jqqdt                                 1/1   Running   0     85s
      kindnet-qpcwf                                 1/1   Running   0     81s
    
    !    kind's default CNI (kindnetd) does NOT enforce NetworkPolicy at all, so a
    !    policy could not be the cause here even if one existed.
    This also matches the error we saw: a policy drop produces a TIMEOUT,
    whereas we got 'Connection refused' (an active TCP RST).

