--- L9  IDENTIFY: root cause ----------------------------------
    Service backend .spec.ports[0].targetPort  = 9090
    backend container .ports[0].containerPort   = 8080
    FAIL MISMATCH  ->  kube-proxy sends traffic to podIP:9090 but nginx listens on :8080

  ROOT CAUSE: the backend Service targetPort (9090) does not match the port
  the backend container actually listens on (8080).  The Service object
  re-points ClusterIP:80 at a closed port, so every frontend -> backend
  connection is rejected with a TCP RST ("Connection refused").
  The pod, the application and DNS are all healthy - only the
  Service -> pod port mapping is wrong.


    run scripts/06-fix.sh to correct the Service, then scripts/07-verify-fixed.sh
